%U A399059 0,8,4,0,4,1,8,2,2,4,2,8,0,3,4,8,0,4
%N A399059 Decimal expansion of Sum_{k>=2} d(k-1)/prime(k)!.
%C A399059 Here d is the number of divisors function (A000005). The constant encodes all primes: it equals the regularized double sum Sum_{n>=1} (f(n) - 1/2) with f(n) = Sum_{i>=0} 1/prime(i*n+1)!; the -1/2 counterterm cancels exactly the divergent i=0 term (which repeats prime(1)=2), so each prime p_k appears with multiplicity d(k-1). The terms decay super-exponentially, so the value is dominated by the first few terms. The denominators of the terms are given in A398118; the constant is the limit of the partial sums of their reciprocals.
%F A399059 Equals Sum_{k>=2} 1/A398118(k) = Sum_{k>=2} A000005(k-1)/A039716(k).
%F A399059 Equals Sum_{m>=1} (f(m) - 1/2), where f(m) = Sum_{j>=0} 1/prime(j*m+1)!; the -1/2 counterterm removes the divergent j=0 term.
%e A399059 0.1837302342076760254907613780132086722793988322673950312...
%o A399059 (PARI) suminf(k=2, numdiv(k-1)/prime(k)!) \\ _Hugo Pfoertner_, Aug 18 2026
